          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong simplex category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            encodes one of the main
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+shapes+for+higher+structures"} geometric shapes for higher structures
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplices"} simplices
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+category"} simplicial category
          %h2#Definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong augmented simplex category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_a
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+categories"} free categories
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
              linear
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graphs"} directed graphs
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{c_0 \to c_1 \to \cdots \to c_n\}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Equivalently, this is the category whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              are finite
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+order"} totally ordered sets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              are order-preserving functions between them.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              As a consequence of the equivalent description,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_a
              can be viewed as a full sub-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-poset"} 2-poset
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pos"} Pos
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong simplex category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_a
              (and hence of
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
              linear directed graphs, hence of
              %em non-empty
              finite linear orders or
              %em non-zero
              ordinals.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              It is common, convenient and without risk to use a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleton"} skeleton
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+class"} isomorphism class
              of objects. Since isomorphisms of finite linearly ordered sets are
              %em unique
              this step is so trivial that it is often not even mentioned explicitly.
            %p
              With this the objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              are in bijection with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              and one usually writes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [n] = \{0 \to 1 \to \cdots \to n\}
            %p
              for the object of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              given by the category with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spine"} spine
              of the standard cellular
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
              %a{:href => "#SimplicialSets"} simplicial sets
              below. In this context one also writes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} represented
              by the object
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              one may identify the subcategory of simplicial sets on the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            %p
              With this convention the first few objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              are
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [0] = \{0\}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [1] = \{0 \to 1\}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [2] = \{0 \to 1 \to 2\}
            %p etc.
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_a
              contains one more object, corresponding to the empty category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [-1] = \emptyset
                    \\,.
            %p
              However, in contexts where only
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_a
              and not
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              plays a role, some authors prefer to start counting with 0 instead of with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{0} = \emptyset
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{1} = [0] =  \{0\}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{2} = [1]  = \{0 \to 1\}
            %p and generally
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{n} = [n-1]
            %p may be used.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleton"} skeletal
              version of the
              %strong augmented simplex category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_a
              can be presented as follows:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  objects are the finite totally ordered sets
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi n
                        %mo ≔
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mn 1
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{n} \coloneqq \{0 \lt 1 \lt  \cdots \lt n-1\}
                  for all
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %li
                %p
                  morphisms
                  %em generated
                  by (are all expressible as finite compositions of) the following two elementary kinds of maps
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      %strong> face maps
                      \:
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %msubsup
                              %mi δ
                              %mi i
                              %mi n
                            %mo :
                            %mspace{:width => "mediummathspace"}
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo ↪
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi n
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;\delta_i^n :\: \mathbf{n-1} \hookrightarrow \mathbf{n}\;
                      is the injection whose image leaves out
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi n
                            %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \mathbf{n}\quad
                      (
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo &gt;
                            %mn 0
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 0
                      and
                      = succeed ");" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mn 0
                              %mo ≤
                              %mi i
                              %mo &lt;
                              %mi n
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq i \lt n
                  %li
                    %p
                      %strong> degeneracy maps
                      \:
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %msubsup
                              %mi σ
                              %mi i
                              %mi n
                            %mo :
                            %mspace{:width => "mediummathspace"}
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo →
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi n
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;\sigma_i^n :\: \mathbf{n+1} \to  \mathbf{n}\;
                      is the surjection such that
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi i
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %mi i
                            %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_i(i) = \sigma_i(i+1) = i\quad
                      (
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo &gt;
                            %mn 0
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 0
                      and
                      = succeed ");" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mn 0
                              %mo ≤
                              %mi i
                              %mo &lt;
                              %mi n
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq i \lt n
            %p
              subject to the following relations, called the
              %strong simplicial relations
              or
              = succeed ":" do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+identities"} simplicial identities
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi δ
                              %mi i
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo ∘
                            %msubsup
                              %mi δ
                              %mi j
                              %mi n
                            %mo =
                            %msubsup
                              %mi δ
                              %mrow
                                %mi j
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo ∘
                            %msubsup
                              %mi δ
                              %mi i
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                            %mi i
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi j
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi σ
                              %mi j
                              %mi n
                            %mo ∘
                            %msubsup
                              %mi σ
                              %mi i
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo =
                            %msubsup
                              %mi σ
                              %mi i
                              %mi n
                            %mo ∘
                            %msubsup
                              %mi σ
                              %mrow
                                %mi j
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                            %mi i
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\delta_i^{n+1} \circ \delta_j^n
                    \=
                    \\delta_{j+1}^{n+1}\circ \delta_i^n
                    \&amp;
                    \\qquad i \leq j
                    \\\
                    \\sigma_j^n \circ \sigma_i^{n+1}
                    \=
                    \\sigma_i^n \circ \sigma_{j+1}^{n+1}
                    \&amp;
                    \\qquad i \leq j
                    }
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi σ
                      %mi j
                      %mi n
                    %mo ∘
                    %msubsup
                      %mi δ
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mi δ
                                %mi i
                                %mi n
                              %mo ∘
                              %msubsup
                                %mi σ
                                %mrow
                                  %mi j
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                                %mrow
                                  %mi n
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                              %mi i
                              %mo &lt;
                              %mi j
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi Id
                                %mi n
                            %mtd
                              %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                              %mi i
                              %mo =
                              %mi j
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi or
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi i
                              %mo =
                              %mi j
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mi δ
                                %mrow
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                                %mi n
                              %mo ∘
                              %msubsup
                                %mi σ
                                %mi j
                                %mrow
                                  %mi n
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                              %mi j
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                              %mo &lt;
                              %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma_j^n \circ \delta_i^{n+1}
                    \=
                    \\left\lbrace
                    \\array{
                    \\delta_i^n \circ \sigma_{j-1}^{n-1}
                    \&amp;
                    \\qquad i \lt j
                    \\\
                    Id_n
                    \&amp;
                    \\qquad i = j \;or\; i = j+1
                    \\\
                    \\delta^n_{i-1} \circ \sigma_{j}^{n-1}
                    \&amp;
                    \\qquad j+1 \lt i
                    }
                    \\right.
            %p
              whenever
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i, j
              are chosen so that the maps are defined. For example, in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi δ
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msubsup
                      %mi δ
                      %mi j
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi δ
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msubsup
                      %mi δ
                      %mi i
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\delta_i^{n+1} \circ \delta_j^n
                    \=
                    \\delta_{j+1}^{n+1}\circ \delta_i^n
            %p
              we implicitly require
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq i, j \leq n
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#ordinal Monoidal structure
          %p
            The addition of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi a
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \oplus : \Delta_a \times \Delta_a \to \Delta_a
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mo :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \oplus : \Delta \times \Delta \to \Delta
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi m
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{m} \oplus \mathbf{n}
            to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            of the underlying sets of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{m}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{n}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{m}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{n}
            by putting every element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{m}
            below every element of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{n}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+sum"} ordinal sum
            functor. If we visualise
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{n}
            as a totally ordered set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 1
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0 \lt 1 \lt \cdots \lt n-1\}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{m}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi m
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{m} \oplus \mathbf{n}
            looks like
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi m
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn 1
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi m
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo &lt;
                  %msup
                    %mn 0
                    %mo *
                  %mo &lt;
                  %msup
                    %mn 1
                    %mo *
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{m} \oplus \mathbf{n} = \{0 \lt 1 \lt  \cdots \lt m-1 \lt 0^*\lt 1^* \lt \cdots \lt (n-1)^*\}
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^*
            denotes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            considered as an element of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{n}
          %p
            Clearly
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi a
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \oplus : \Delta_a \times \Delta_a \to \Delta_a
            acts on objects as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi m
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi m
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{n} \oplus \mathbf{m} = \mathbf{n+m},
          %p
            On morphisms, given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi m
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi m
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : \mathbf{m} \to \mathbf{m}'
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi n
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : \mathbf{n} \to \mathbf{n}'
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi if
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi i
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi m
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi m
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi i
                            %mo −
                            %mi m
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi if
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi m
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi i
                            %mo ≤
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi m
                            %mo +
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (f\oplus g)(i) = \left\lbrace
                  \\array{
                  f(i) &amp; if \; 0 \leq i  \leq m - 1
                  \\\
                  m' + g(i-m) &amp; if \; m \leq i \leq (m+n-1)
                  }
                  \\right.
                  \\,.
          %p
            so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \oplus g
            can be visualised as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            placed side by side.
          %p
            It is easy to see now that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Delta_a,\oplus,\mathbf{0})
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+monoidal+category"} strict monoidal category
          %p
            It is important to note that this tensor does
            %em not
            give a monoidal structure to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{0} = [-1] = \emptyset
          %p
            Also note that this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+structure"} monoidal structure
            is
            %em not
            = succeed "!" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+category"} braided
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi m
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi n
                  %mo ≃
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi m
                  %mo ≃
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{m} \oplus \mathbf{n} \simeq \mathbf{n+m} \simeq \mathbf{n} \oplus \mathbf{m}
            for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m,n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{n+m}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifunctorial"} bifunctorial
          %p
            Under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            this monoidal structure induces the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join+of+simplicial+sets"} join of simplicial sets
          %h3#As2Categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_a
            as 2-categories
          %p
            Being full subcategories of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_a
            are themselves 2-categories: their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-cell"} 2-cells
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \Rightarrow g
            are given by the pointwise order on monotone functions. Equivalently, they are generated under (vertical and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+composition"} horizontal
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi δ
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %mo ≤
                  %msubsup
                    %mi δ
                    %mi i
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi σ
                    %mi i
                    %mi n
                  %mo ≤
                  %msubsup
                    %mi σ
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta^n_{i+1} \leq \delta^n_i \qquad \qquad \sigma^n_i \leq \sigma^n_{i+1} \, .
          %p
            Of course, the ordinal sum functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊕
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \oplus
            extends to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor"} 2-functor
            in the obvious way.
          %p
            For each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            there is
            %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/adjoint+string"} a string of adjunctions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi δ
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msubsup
                    %mi σ
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msubsup
                    %mi δ
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msubsup
                    %mi δ
                    %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msubsup
                    %mi σ
                    %mn 0
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msubsup
                    %mi δ
                    %mn 0
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\delta^n_{n-1} \dashv \sigma^n_{n-2} \dashv \delta^n_{n-2} \dashv
                  \\cdots \dashv \delta^n_1 \dashv \sigma^n_0 \dashv \delta^n_0
          %p
            where the counit of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mi i
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_i \dashv \delta_i
            and the unit of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_{i+1} \dashv \sigma_i
            are identities.
          %p
            For each
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{n+1}
            is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi δ
                                %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi n
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                            %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "1"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi δ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi n
                                    %mo −
                                    %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "1"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi δ
                                  %mi n
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi n
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi δ
                                %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{n-1} &amp; \overset{\delta_0}{\to} &amp; \mathbf{n} \\
                  \\mathllap{\scriptsize{\delta_{n-1}}} \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{\scriptsize{\delta_n}} \\
                  \\mathbf{n} &amp; \underset{\delta_0}{\to} &amp; \mathbf{n+1}
                  }
          %p
            This means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_a
            is generated as a 2-category by these pushouts and by taking adjoints of morphisms. Its monoidal structure is also determined in this way: for each
            = succeed "," do
